</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Recency-Window Sweeps</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The recency-window sweep in Table <a href="#S3.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 3.3 Ablation Studies ‣ 3 Experiments ‣ Compress What You See, Not What You Say: Anchored Context Distillation for Latent-Observation Software Engineering Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>a is detailed in Table <a href="#A3.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ C.2 Recency-Window Sweeps ‣ Appendix C Per-Seed Results and Recency-Window Sweeps ‣ Compress What You See, Not What You Say: Anchored Context Distillation for Latent-Observation Software Engineering Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>. Each condition uses one run, with one final result per instance.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T10" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 10: </span>Recency-window sweeps, one run per condition. Left: Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507, 200-iteration cap, 262K context. Right: SWE-Master-4B-RL, 100-iteration cap, 131K context. Resolved counts are out of 499; dec PF is estimated decoder compute per trajectory.</figcaption>
